infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Same leaked dump, two attacker economics
  desc Fast hash vs tuned KDF — the asymmetry is the whole point of a KDF
  compares
    - label Fast hash (SHA-256 / MD5)
      children
        - label ~Billions of guesses/sec
          desc GPU brute-forces a leaked dump offline, no rate limit
        - label Unsalted: rainbow tables
          desc Identical passwords share a digest, crack once match many
        - label Built for speed
          desc Exactly the property that helps the attacker
    - label Tuned scrypt KDF
      children
        - label ~Thousands of guesses/sec
          desc Slow + memory-hard makes every guess expensive
        - label Per-password salt
          desc Every hash is unique, so rainbow tables die
        - label Cost factor raised over years
          desc Async form keeps the event loop unblocked
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
